From db1416d15be17e089e4b9c430069a2d1aec779fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:01:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ci: scripts executable again; the docs gate green
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two of the three stages `ci/check/checks.sh --quick` failed on 1.98.1.

- web-sys feature audit: "Permission denied". 30 of the 32 shebang
  scripts under ci/ (and .github/workflows-pending/restore.sh) were
  stored as 100644 — the exec bits were lost when the tree was uploaded
  through the web — so checks.sh's direct `ci/check/wasm-check.sh` call
  failed on every machine. Modes restored (the two sourced libraries,
  ci/lib/lean.sh and ci/mobile/android-env.sh, stay 644), and the call
  now goes through `bash` so a lost bit cannot break the gate again.
  .cargo/config.toml's NDK linker shims and adb/simctl runners are
  executed by cargo directly and needed the bit too.
- docs (`-D warnings`): 24 broken intra-doc links across vieww-3d,
  vieww-canvas, vieww-dataviz, vieww-gpu, vieww-hal, vieww-platform-
  winit, vieww-video, vieww-widget and film_lab — redundant explicit
  targets, links to private items, links to a feature-gated module,
  a renamed brush, and maths/paths (`[0,1]²`, `w3[i]`, `<name>`) that
  rustdoc read as links or HTML. Doc text only; the full docs stage
  now passes.

The third failure (wait_loop's idle scenario timing out on the
developer's desktop) passes 3/3 here under Xvfb + lavapipe and needs a
trace from the machine where it hung.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nd3Ehrf9ktGu82K38kGEjH
